I am very cold now.
My hands are cold.
I look around the market.
I see a small coffee cart.
A young man stands behind the cart.
I walk over to him.
I say hello to the barista.
"Hello, how much does a black coffee cost?" I ask.
The barista smiles.
"A hot, black coffee costs thirty kroner," he answers.
I have coins in my coat pocket.
It is my change from the apples.
I take the coins out.
I count them.
I have exactly thirty kroner.
"Here you go, here are thirty kroner," I say.
He takes the money.
He gives me the hot coffee.
The coffee smells wonderful.
I warm my hands on the cup.
